  "result": "Perfect! All 192 tests pass. Here's what I've implemented:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Added payment terms support to invoices:**\n\n**Updated `createInvoice()` function:**\n- Accepts optional `terms` parameter: `'NET14'`, `'NET30'` (default), or `'EOM'`\n- Returns `fail('TERMS_INVALID')` for unknown terms\n- Sets `invoice.terms` and `invoice.dueDate` on the created invoice\n- Terms are case-sensitive and must match exactly\n\n**Due date calculation:**\n- **NET14**: invoice due 14 days after issue date\n  - Example: issued 2024-03-15 \u2192 due 2024-03-29\n- **NET30**: invoice due 30 days after issue date (default)\n  - Example: issued 2024-03-15 \u2192 due 2024-04-14\n- **EOM**: invoice due on last day of issue date's month\n  - Example: issued 2024-03-15 \u2192 due 2024-03-31\n  - Handles month lengths correctly (28/29/30/31 days)\n  - Handles year boundaries (December \u2192 January of next year)\n\n**Added TERMS_INVALID error code** for unrecognized payment terms\n\n**Added 10 comprehensive tests** covering:\n- Default NET30 terms applied automatically\n- NET14 term calculation\n- NET30 term calculation\n- EOM term calculation\n- EOM with February (leap year: Feb 29, non-leap year: Feb 28)\n- EOM with December (year boundary)\n- EOM with 30-day month\n- EOM with 31-day month\n- Invalid terms rejection\n- Case-sensitive validation\n\nAll 192 tests pass \u2705",
